> Note: everything you pasted is from the "proposal to change {da'o}"
> section, not its main definition. It's not clear to me how close the
> proposal is to being implemented.
>
> On Tuesday, December 2, 2014 at 5:26 AM, Gleki Arxokuna wrote:
>
> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/BPFK+Section%3A+Reference+Regulators
>
> *1) da'o is moved to selma'o UI. DAhO is almost UI anyway. *
>
>
>
> *3) da'inai means this: the variable da'onai is attached to retains its
> assignment and all other variables are cleared. *
>
> This is a mistype. It should be {da'onai}
>
> Yep.
>
>
> *4) da'oda'o means that all variables have their assignments cleared.*
>
> This contradicts with how UI work. This can no longer be UI or UI becomes
> impractical from the viewpoint of parsers.
>
>
> It's a semantics issue, not a parser issue. Seems fine to me.
>

Depends on what parser you are talking about.
It create a new semantic class, the behavior of which is completely new and
unique. That's what the problem.

It's better not to smash everything into one selma'o if they differ in
behavior.

